segments: Environmental Services and Safety-Kleen Sustainability Solutions. The Environmental Services segment collects, transports, treats, recycles, and disposes hazardous and non-hazardous waste, such as resource recovery, physical treatment, incineration, landfill disposal, wastewater treatment, lab chemicals disposal, and explosives management services; and offers CleanPack services, including collection, identification, categorization, specialized packaging, transportation, and disposal of laboratory chemicals and household hazardous waste. This segment also provides industrial maintenance and specialty industrial services; and utilizes specialty equipment and resources that perform field services. The Safety-Kleen Sustainability Solutions segment provides containerized waste, parts-washer, and vacuum services for automobile repair shops, car and truck dealers, metal fabricators, machine manufacturers, fleet maintenance shops, and other automotive, industrial, and retail customers; collects and transports for hazardous and non-hazardous containerized waste for recycling or disposal; machine cleaning and maintenance, and disposal and replenishment of clean solvent or aqueous fluids; and vacuum services to remove solids, residual oily water, and sludge and other fluids from customers' oil/water separators, sumps, and collection tanks, as well as removes and collects waste fluids found at large and small industrial locations, including metal fabricators, auto maintenance providers, and general manufacturers. This segment also manufactures, formulates, and packages lubricants and other products. Clean Harbors, Inc. was incorporated in 1980 and is headquartered in Norwell, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eric W. Gerstenberg | Co-CEO, Co-President & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22K people. Revenue per employee of $272K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Clean Harbors, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $15.0B market cap on $6.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $442M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.22\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.06838451090971694},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (75% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.25},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Clean Harbors (NYSE:CLH) Price Target Raised to $379.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/clean-harbors-nyseclh-price-target-raised-to-379-00.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793862769.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Clean Harbors (CLH) \u2013 Investment Analysts\u2019 Recent Ratings Updates","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/clean-harbors-clh-investment-analysts-recent-ratings-updates.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793712418.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CLH Q3 deep dive: emergency response and refined products drive margin expansion, CEO transition ahead","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/clh-q3-deep-dive-emergency-072536960.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793690736.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","leadership"]},{"title":"Clean Harbors Stock Slides 6% Since Posting Q3 Earnings & Revenue Beat","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023373/clean-harbo