ents":{"decline":{"score":0.014,"weight":0.25},"balance_sheet":{"score":0.188,"weight":0.2},"value_destruction":{"score":0.39,"weight":0.2},"derating":{"score":0.355,"weight":0.15},"market":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 11% operating margin is roughly in line with the Industrials median (9%).","Its share of sector profits slightly exceeds its share of revenue (1.01x).","It accounts for 0.2% of sector revenue and 0.2% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been gaining share of the sector profit pool (+8.5% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.01 across 544 companies in the universe; the top four hold 9% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 55% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 10% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 15% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 25% and a beta of 0.78, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.20 vs 5y 0.74), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $134.6M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 65% in the 2020 crash, 27% in the 2022 bear market and 50% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $266 (margin of safety -7%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 40%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $159 to $437 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/FCF 33.9 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 28% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 2.9% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 15 covering analysts target $367 on average, 29% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 10% earns above the cost of capital of 8.0%, but the 2pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.59).","It converts 7% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.22x.","ROE of 14% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.5% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.5x net debt to EBITDA ($516.6M of cash against $2.8B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 4.3x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.33)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.3% over 3 years, 13.9% over 5 years and 6.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","At current returns, reinvesting 32% of profits supports about 3.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 13.5% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 8%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.0x, 7.0% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.9%, and institutions hold 96%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 3 sales over the past year, net $1.2M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.7% (1.7% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 0.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 22,155 employees, each generates about $272K of revenue, 0.7x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 8.7% a year.","That works out to $20K of free cash flow per employee.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $2.7M (10x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $1K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":59,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $226.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 41, gates 9/26)","Revenue grew 13.9%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone","15 analysts' mean target $367 (+29%)","12-1 month momentum +55%"],"cons":["Trades 7% above fair value of $266","P/FCF 33.9x vs sector 22.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":226.03,"vc":{"base":265.92,"base_src":"dcf","bear":158.98,"bull":437.18,"alt_median":78.25,"n_alt":2,"gap":2.3984,"dispersion":0.3985,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (40% dispersion)","DCF is 240% above the other models' median ($78.25)"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"CLH","date":"2026-11-06"}